WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.344
- Brendon, you want to be a writer?

00:00:01.344 --> 00:00:02.498
You can't write!

00:00:02.498 --> 00:00:05.337
You have to actually take an
action that moves you forward.

00:00:05.337 --> 00:00:07.228
Getting very clear on the mission.

00:00:07.228 --> 00:00:09.872
I think doubt is one of the
greatest enemies of our lives.

00:00:09.872 --> 00:00:11.958
So if you don't want to go to
a meeting, sit down and say,

00:00:11.958 --> 00:00:14.429
guys, I have 45 minutes
today for this meeting.

00:00:14.429 --> 00:00:18.498
The time to have the map is
before you enter the woods.

00:00:18.498 --> 00:00:20.524
Get back in the game where
you have a community of people

00:00:20.524 --> 00:00:23.401
who are giving you advanced
feedback before you release it.

00:00:23.401 --> 00:00:25.334
You just start trying
to live a life that's

00:00:25.334 --> 00:00:26.658
not even our own.

00:00:26.658 --> 00:00:28.141
I had, nobody had ever really told me

00:00:28.141 --> 00:00:29.666
I had any potential before.

00:00:29.666 --> 00:00:31.398
I have to change myself.

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:34.725
- He's an American author on
motivation, high performance,

00:00:34.725 --> 00:00:36.210
and online marketing.

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:38.269
He's the founder of the Experts Academy

00:00:38.269 --> 00:00:40.077
and High Performance Academy.

00:00:40.077 --> 00:00:42.844
He's the number one New York
Times bestselling author

00:00:42.844 --> 00:00:44.651
of The Millionaire Messenger.

00:00:44.651 --> 00:00:46.380
He's Brendon Burchard and here are his

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:47.942
top 10 rules for success.

00:00:47.942 --> 00:00:51.531
(dramatic sibilant music)

00:00:51.531 --> 00:00:54.231
- No matter where you are
in accomplishing your dreams

00:00:54.231 --> 00:00:57.356
or moving towards the things
that you really want in life,

00:00:57.356 --> 00:01:02.050
never let your small beginnings
make you small minded.

00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:05.670
It's easy to say, well, that's impossible.

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:06.989
And I know lots of people
are telling you that,

00:01:06.989 --> 00:01:08.346
that's impossible.

00:01:08.346 --> 00:01:09.208
Do you know how many people told me

00:01:09.208 --> 00:01:10.769
what I'm doing today is impossible?

00:01:10.769 --> 00:01:11.798
Brendon, you want to be a writer?

00:01:11.798 --> 00:01:13.032
You can't write!

00:01:13.032 --> 00:01:15.826
Brendon, you want to be a
trainer, you want to be a speaker,

00:01:15.826 --> 00:01:17.352
you want to do YouTube videos?

00:01:17.352 --> 00:01:19.083
You're not good on video,
you're not good at this,

00:01:19.083 --> 00:01:20.402
you're not good at this, it's impossible,

00:01:20.402 --> 00:01:23.246
oh, you don't understand how
hard it is to make it, Brendon.

00:01:23.246 --> 00:01:24.444
It's so hard these days.

00:01:24.444 --> 00:01:28.545
The stuff that people tell
me and I know have told you

00:01:28.545 --> 00:01:32.747
is so nonsensical and based
on so many of their own fears

00:01:32.747 --> 00:01:36.080
that have been unexplored that it's sad.

00:01:37.896 --> 00:01:40.327
And it can really cause
great people to stop

00:01:40.327 --> 00:01:42.961
trying to do great things.

00:01:42.961 --> 00:01:45.718
So I want to encourage you,
no matter where you are,

00:01:45.718 --> 00:01:50.238
believe in yourself, keep at
it, keep working, keep going.

00:01:50.238 --> 00:01:52.346
I mean, success and fulfillment
are going to come from your

00:01:52.346 --> 00:01:54.413
unflagging ability to believe in what

00:01:54.413 --> 00:01:56.604
other people call impossible.

00:01:56.604 --> 00:01:59.068
It's going to come from your
unflagging ability to get up

00:01:59.068 --> 00:02:01.500
each day and work towards
things that maybe you don't know

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:02.631
where they're going.

00:02:02.631 --> 00:02:05.182
Maybe they're not getting
you what you want right away.

00:02:05.182 --> 00:02:08.222
Maybe it's not easy,
maybe it is a struggle,

00:02:08.222 --> 00:02:10.573
but it is through that
struggle and that effort

00:02:10.573 --> 00:02:13.042
and that dream and the
desire that you get there.

00:02:13.042 --> 00:02:17.618
You have to actually show up
everyday and inch yourself

00:02:17.618 --> 00:02:20.781
forward toward these dreams.

00:02:20.781 --> 00:02:22.774
And not only show up
everyday and once in a while

00:02:22.774 --> 00:02:26.846
inch yourself, I mean everyday
you have to actually take

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:28.747
an action that moves you forward.

00:02:28.747 --> 00:02:31.058
Not just research, not just thinking.

00:02:31.058 --> 00:02:33.855
Look, the power of intention
is great but without

00:02:33.855 --> 00:02:36.477
any initiative it's dead, right?

00:02:36.477 --> 00:02:40.501
A dream is great but without
any movement, it's dead.

00:02:40.501 --> 00:02:43.503
You have to be moving towards it everyday.

00:02:43.503 --> 00:02:44.724
You can send an email everyday,

00:02:44.724 --> 00:02:46.467
you can make a call everyday,

00:02:46.467 --> 00:02:48.001
you can write something everyday,

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:49.257
you can create something everyday,

00:02:49.257 --> 00:02:50.231
you can contribute something everyday,

00:02:50.231 --> 00:02:52.585
but it has to be daily.

00:02:52.585 --> 00:02:56.070
Otherwise it will never become actualized.

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:57.610
The highest performers in
the world didn't get there

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:58.742
because they were lucky.

00:02:58.742 --> 00:03:01.338
They worked at it longer
than everyone else.

00:03:01.338 --> 00:03:03.567
They had a better work ethic
and it's not that they didn't

00:03:03.567 --> 00:03:06.442
necessarily always worked
harder, they worked smarter

00:03:06.442 --> 00:03:08.752
because they were doing the research,

00:03:08.752 --> 00:03:11.020
they were taking the time
to visual how they would be

00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:14.710
distinct, different, how they
would survive the tough times.

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:16.815
They really kept at it.

00:03:16.815 --> 00:03:19.898
Keep every single day momentum going.

00:03:21.193 --> 00:03:23.257
And if you don't do
that, there's no chance.

00:03:23.257 --> 00:03:25.674
You must define your mission.

00:03:26.783 --> 00:03:29.784
You need to have a mission
for what you're doing today.

00:03:29.784 --> 00:03:32.545
You need to have an intention
for what your next task

00:03:32.545 --> 00:03:33.477
is going to be.

00:03:33.477 --> 00:03:35.177
What happens is most
people just kind of show up

00:03:35.177 --> 00:03:37.649
and they go, okay, well,
I guess I'll do some stuff

00:03:37.649 --> 00:03:41.461
but they have no intention
whatsoever so they end up doing

00:03:41.461 --> 00:03:45.521
too many things that mean
nothing towards their mission.

00:03:45.521 --> 00:03:47.918
You should figure out what
is it you desire in life?

00:03:47.918 --> 00:03:49.744
And figure out the steps to get there

00:03:49.744 --> 00:03:52.258
and start working a plan
to get there and minimizing

00:03:52.258 --> 00:03:55.863
everything else, getting
very clear on the mission.

00:03:55.863 --> 00:03:59.596
Very clear on the mission
and working the plan.

00:03:59.596 --> 00:04:01.909
Everything else, guess what it gets?

00:04:01.909 --> 00:04:03.085
A no.

00:04:03.085 --> 00:04:05.556
Until you reach that mission
or until you're significantly

00:04:05.556 --> 00:04:08.724
on your way that you have
free resources to be able

00:04:08.724 --> 00:04:10.099
to focus elsewhere.

00:04:10.099 --> 00:04:11.316
And that's what people do.

00:04:11.316 --> 00:04:13.419
They take on too many
projects because they're not

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:14.918
clear about their mission.

00:04:14.918 --> 00:04:16.740
Because, I'm guessing, if
you're watching this, you know,

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:19.630
you're somebody who wants to
add value and make a difference

00:04:19.630 --> 00:04:20.463
in the world.

00:04:20.463 --> 00:04:22.304
So, anytime someone asks you
to do something you're like,

00:04:22.304 --> 00:04:23.804
yeah, let me help you.

00:04:23.804 --> 00:04:26.351
But that might not have
anything to do with the quality

00:04:26.351 --> 00:04:29.828
of life or the objective or
the thing that you're trying

00:04:29.828 --> 00:04:33.193
to achieve or the service you're
really intending to offer.

00:04:33.193 --> 00:04:34.083
Right?

00:04:34.083 --> 00:04:37.531
And I know how hard it is
because I'm so pulled myself

00:04:37.531 --> 00:04:40.127
towards causes and towards
volunteerism and towards helping

00:04:40.127 --> 00:04:40.960
so many people.

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:41.793
But guess what?

00:04:41.793 --> 00:04:44.095
If I help everybody in
lots of different areas,

00:04:44.095 --> 00:04:48.344
I might not make my ultimate
mission of serving the people

00:04:48.344 --> 00:04:50.293
I want to serve the most.

00:04:50.293 --> 00:04:54.059
Of making my dreams comes true
so I can support more people,

00:04:54.059 --> 00:04:56.389
of running my business so
I can support more people.

00:04:56.389 --> 00:04:59.348
Meaning it's easy to take
your eye off the ball

00:04:59.348 --> 00:05:02.553
if you don't know what the ball is.

00:05:02.553 --> 00:05:05.262
And people often have never
defined their mission.

00:05:05.262 --> 00:05:07.534
And if you don't have one
right now, for this day,

00:05:07.534 --> 00:05:10.778
if you didn't have a drive,
a mission, a written down

00:05:10.778 --> 00:05:12.732
statement about what you're
going to accomplish today,

00:05:12.732 --> 00:05:16.379
a checklist, a goal sheet,
a time management tool

00:05:16.379 --> 00:05:18.644
that you filled out today and
you're just showing up today

00:05:18.644 --> 00:05:20.831
and going, well, I guess I'll
see what my inbox tells me

00:05:20.831 --> 00:05:21.888
to do today.

00:05:21.888 --> 00:05:24.805
And you just respond to
everybody else's desires

00:05:24.805 --> 00:05:26.995
and everyone else's emails
and you're just always

00:05:26.995 --> 00:05:29.721
in reaction, always
responding to everybody,

00:05:29.721 --> 00:05:33.408
no proactivity towards a mission
that you defined yourself,

00:05:33.408 --> 00:05:34.658
you'll be lost.

00:05:35.917 --> 00:05:39.853
You'll find that because you
never focused on that one

00:05:39.853 --> 00:05:42.365
thing or moving towards those
several things that were

00:05:42.365 --> 00:05:45.448
your priority, that you're just lost.

00:05:46.462 --> 00:05:47.799
Because here's another thing.

00:05:47.799 --> 00:05:52.438
Focus goes out the window
when we don't have progress.

00:05:52.438 --> 00:05:53.271
Right?

00:05:53.271 --> 00:05:54.815
If we're not progressing
towards something,

00:05:54.815 --> 00:05:56.116
our focus goes out the window.

00:05:56.116 --> 00:05:57.705
We just don't pay attention to anything.

00:05:57.705 --> 00:05:59.375
We don't feel good about ourselves.

00:05:59.375 --> 00:06:02.130
You want to get more focus in
your life, get more progress.

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:03.915
As you progress more,
you start to get excited,

00:06:03.915 --> 00:06:05.941
you start to pay attention to
the things that are working

00:06:05.941 --> 00:06:07.969
that are moving you forward
and you start to find

00:06:07.969 --> 00:06:09.469
more focus in your life.

00:06:09.469 --> 00:06:12.229
The first enemy we all have is doubt.

00:06:12.229 --> 00:06:15.228
You know, we doubt whether
or not we're capable,

00:06:15.228 --> 00:06:16.766
we doubt whether or not we're worthy,

00:06:16.766 --> 00:06:18.674
we doubt whether or not we'll succeed,

00:06:18.674 --> 00:06:22.031
we doubt whether or
not we even deserve it,

00:06:22.031 --> 00:06:24.057
and it's so unfortunate
because I think doubt is

00:06:24.057 --> 00:06:26.040
one of the greatest enemies of our lives.

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:30.251
And it's so easy to overcome
but most people won't practice

00:06:30.251 --> 00:06:33.322
the discipline of overcoming
it, which is weird, right?

00:06:33.322 --> 00:06:36.289
They say, oh, I'm so
doubtful, and they stop.

00:06:36.289 --> 00:06:38.807
And it's like, if you have
any negative recurring emotion

00:06:38.807 --> 00:06:39.744
in your life,

00:06:39.744 --> 00:06:42.302
doesn't maturity require
you to face it and say,

00:06:42.302 --> 00:06:45.021
hey, how do I fix this?

00:06:45.021 --> 00:06:45.854
You know?

00:06:45.854 --> 00:06:47.822
If you're always doubtful,
you can't just wander around

00:06:47.822 --> 00:06:50.810
saying, oh, I'm so doubtful,
like some kind of victim.

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:53.289
That's not fair to the
humanity you've been given,

00:06:53.289 --> 00:06:56.687
that real power of free
will that says, hey,

00:06:56.687 --> 00:06:58.875
you can direct your
consciousness, that's why you have

00:06:58.875 --> 00:07:00.940
this big prefrontal cortex.

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:02.851
Other animals can't, we can.

00:07:02.851 --> 00:07:04.473
So, handle it.

00:07:04.473 --> 00:07:06.754
If you've been plagued
with doubt your whole life,

00:07:06.754 --> 00:07:10.035
then face it, stop running from it.

00:07:10.035 --> 00:07:11.607
I know that sounds hard
to say to people but I had

00:07:11.607 --> 00:07:12.947
the same story.

00:07:12.947 --> 00:07:16.477
I was so doubtful that people
would care about what I say.

00:07:16.477 --> 00:07:19.066
I was so doubtful that people
would want to read my books

00:07:19.066 --> 00:07:20.227
or listen to me at all.

00:07:20.227 --> 00:07:22.132
I was so doubtful that I
could chase my own dreams

00:07:22.132 --> 00:07:26.061
then I realized, for what
reason am I doubtful.

00:07:26.061 --> 00:07:27.891
Because of past failures in this space?

00:07:27.891 --> 00:07:29.510
No, I'm trying something new.

00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:32.141
Because people told me I
might not be able to do it?

00:07:32.141 --> 00:07:35.483
So, what makes them an
expert on my capabilities

00:07:35.483 --> 00:07:37.427
and my potentialities?

00:07:37.427 --> 00:07:39.735
I thought, well, why am I so doubtful?

00:07:39.735 --> 00:07:44.558
We're doubtful because the
germ of fear spread in our body

00:07:44.558 --> 00:07:47.473
because somebody planted it
there one time or we cultivate

00:07:47.473 --> 00:07:49.580
it with our own thoughts.

00:07:49.580 --> 00:07:52.528
And at some point maturity
and consciousness says

00:07:52.528 --> 00:07:55.766
if doubt has been plaguing
you, let's have a look at it.

00:07:55.766 --> 00:07:58.026
And let's realize, well,
how do you banish it?

00:07:58.026 --> 00:08:02.326
Well, every single thing that
we know from spirituality,

00:08:02.326 --> 00:08:05.488
from philosophy, from the great
writers and the great texts

00:08:05.488 --> 00:08:08.764
of human culture has
all revealed one thing.

00:08:08.764 --> 00:08:12.092
Where there is doubt, grant me faith.

00:08:12.092 --> 00:08:14.202
That we have to have faith.

00:08:14.202 --> 00:08:16.143
And faith does not mean
the absence of doubt.

00:08:16.143 --> 00:08:19.382
Matter of fact, the very
definition of faith relies that

00:08:19.382 --> 00:08:21.133
doubt is still there, right?

00:08:21.133 --> 00:08:23.323
You can't have faith unless
there's some part of you

00:08:23.323 --> 00:08:26.276
that says, well, I'm going to
go anyway despite the doubt.

00:08:26.276 --> 00:08:29.279
So I'm not saying that we have
to get rid of doubt forever

00:08:29.279 --> 00:08:30.112
and handle it.

00:08:30.112 --> 00:08:33.053
I'm saying doubt should never
prevent you from advancing

00:08:33.053 --> 00:08:36.053
when you feel like advancing.

00:08:36.053 --> 00:08:38.210
That in your own mind you must say, okay,

00:08:38.210 --> 00:08:40.405
I must trust in my abilities,

00:08:40.405 --> 00:08:42.473
I must trust that I will figure it out,

00:08:42.473 --> 00:08:44.131
I must trust that I can build it,

00:08:44.131 --> 00:08:46.561
I must trust that I can get some help,

00:08:46.561 --> 00:08:50.369
and progress even though
the doubt might be there.

00:08:50.369 --> 00:08:53.690
Look, the hero is a hero
because the hero does it anyway.

00:08:53.690 --> 00:08:54.523
Right?

00:08:54.523 --> 00:08:57.254
Even though the hero is
terrified and risking it all,

00:08:57.254 --> 00:08:59.971
goes anyway and we're
all heroes in some way.

00:08:59.971 --> 00:09:01.548
We can all be courageous.

00:09:01.548 --> 00:09:04.591
But I also think society
overblows courage.

00:09:04.591 --> 00:09:07.318
Society says, you know,
courage has to be some big

00:09:07.318 --> 00:09:10.033
magnificent act but it's not.

00:09:10.033 --> 00:09:12.589
I mean, courage in this
world, anymore, is just having

00:09:12.589 --> 00:09:16.853
the belief in yourself and
having the ability to genuinely

00:09:16.853 --> 00:09:18.520
express who you are.

00:09:19.895 --> 00:09:22.413
If you're doubting yourself,
the only way through

00:09:22.413 --> 00:09:26.105
is to give yourself more
faith and take more action.

00:09:26.105 --> 00:09:30.557
And with more faith and more
action comes more competence.

00:09:30.557 --> 00:09:32.990
With more competence
comes more confidence.

00:09:32.990 --> 00:09:33.928
In psychology, they call it

00:09:33.928 --> 00:09:36.484
the competence/confidence loop, right?

00:09:36.484 --> 00:09:39.766
The more you learn and try, the
more you master and develop.

00:09:39.766 --> 00:09:43.208
So, go out there, even without,
yes, let the doubt be there,

00:09:43.208 --> 00:09:44.591
but do it anyway.

00:09:44.591 --> 00:09:48.522
Be more explicit in
communicating your boundaries.

00:09:48.522 --> 00:09:50.913
Be more explicit in
communicating your time.

00:09:50.913 --> 00:09:52.658
So if you don't want to go to
a meeting, sit down and say,

00:09:52.658 --> 00:09:55.577
guys, I have 45 minutes
today for this meeting.

00:09:55.577 --> 00:09:57.118
I can't go a second over.

00:09:57.118 --> 00:09:59.060
And they're like, oh, okay.

00:09:59.060 --> 00:10:01.132
And stop going over on your times.

00:10:01.132 --> 00:10:02.682
If you said you were going
to work out for an hour,

00:10:02.682 --> 00:10:04.788
work out for an hour, stop, go.

00:10:04.788 --> 00:10:07.873
A lot of the what I
call bleed time ends up

00:10:07.873 --> 00:10:09.536
taking away from our balance.

00:10:09.536 --> 00:10:13.263
Bleed time is those things
where you go over on things

00:10:13.263 --> 00:10:15.329
that you didn't need to go over on.

00:10:15.329 --> 00:10:18.122
You know, that one cocktail
with your friend ended up

00:10:18.122 --> 00:10:22.097
being 16, you know, and you
lost the entire night now.

00:10:22.097 --> 00:10:25.014
Or that one lunch meeting you
were going to have turned into

00:10:25.014 --> 00:10:28.093
four hours and now you've
lost the day of work.

00:10:28.093 --> 00:10:30.398
Or that one show you were
going to watch before getting

00:10:30.398 --> 00:10:33.034
back to work turned into a whole season.

00:10:33.034 --> 00:10:34.615
And you're like, oh, no!

00:10:34.615 --> 00:10:37.291
The day, the night is gone!

00:10:37.291 --> 00:10:39.195
That's called bleed time.

00:10:39.195 --> 00:10:41.509
It's where so much time
just dissipates because

00:10:41.509 --> 00:10:43.495
you didn't stick to your mark.

00:10:43.495 --> 00:10:46.050
So, set your boundary,
communicate it clear with people,

00:10:46.050 --> 00:10:48.730
and don't go over on things anymore.

00:10:48.730 --> 00:10:51.400
A lot of people, if they just
started with the intention

00:10:51.400 --> 00:10:53.424
said, we're only going to
do this for this much time

00:10:53.424 --> 00:10:55.776
and then we got to go,
if they stuck to that,

00:10:55.776 --> 00:10:57.840
they would get better balance.

00:10:57.840 --> 00:10:59.581
If you're really going to get ahead,

00:10:59.581 --> 00:11:02.132
you have to study your craft.

00:11:02.132 --> 00:11:03.836
You have to deeply study it.

00:11:03.836 --> 00:11:07.384
You know, I decided, what
was it now, 18 years ago that

00:11:07.384 --> 00:11:09.816
I wanted to help inspire and
motivate people and I wanted

00:11:09.816 --> 00:11:11.518
to coach people one-on-one on motivation

00:11:11.518 --> 00:11:13.754
and on high performance
and I wanted to write books

00:11:13.754 --> 00:11:15.049
on the topics.

00:11:15.049 --> 00:11:19.422
So, 18 years ago, I started
reading a book a week

00:11:19.422 --> 00:11:23.026
on psychology, leadership,
communication, marketing,

00:11:23.026 --> 00:11:25.174
anything I could get in my
hands about human behavior

00:11:25.174 --> 00:11:26.266
and high performance.

00:11:26.266 --> 00:11:28.248
I was studying everything
I could on psychology

00:11:28.248 --> 00:11:29.301
every single week.

00:11:29.301 --> 00:11:31.127
Now, it's like people, like wait,

00:11:31.127 --> 00:11:32.540
you've read a book a week for 17 years?

00:11:32.540 --> 00:11:33.838
And I don't brag about it.

00:11:33.838 --> 00:11:35.292
I'm not like, oh yeah, look at me.

00:11:35.292 --> 00:11:37.478
That was for my passion.

00:11:37.478 --> 00:11:40.318
I knew if I really wanted
to succeed at something

00:11:40.318 --> 00:11:43.553
I had to study it and I
had to study it deeply.

00:11:43.553 --> 00:11:45.824
And I couldn't, you know,
spend all this time doing all

00:11:45.824 --> 00:11:48.088
the other things, so I
had to study my craft.

00:11:48.088 --> 00:11:51.533
The great artists of our past
history, that's what they did.

00:11:51.533 --> 00:11:52.627
They did one thing.

00:11:52.627 --> 00:11:56.279
They had a true level of
depth of study in that area.

00:11:56.279 --> 00:11:58.312
Now, maybe they dabbled
in some other areas, too,

00:11:58.312 --> 00:12:01.147
but they became famous
because they studied one area.

00:12:01.147 --> 00:12:02.769
And so what's your area?

00:12:02.769 --> 00:12:04.633
What's the thing you need to study on?

00:12:04.633 --> 00:12:07.595
Develop a deep level of
competence into how to do it

00:12:07.595 --> 00:12:09.261
and how that world works.

00:12:09.261 --> 00:12:11.202
Because, you know, we have
this saying in Montana

00:12:11.202 --> 00:12:16.186
that the time to have the map
is before you enter the woods.

00:12:16.186 --> 00:12:18.371
But a lot of people have
a dream and they run out

00:12:18.371 --> 00:12:20.400
into the woods and they
just start trying stuff

00:12:20.400 --> 00:12:22.263
and they take this path, and
this path, and this path,

00:12:22.263 --> 00:12:26.480
and this path, and because they
didn't study best practices,

00:12:26.480 --> 00:12:29.768
they some day they wake
up and they're lost,

00:12:29.768 --> 00:12:32.279
they're confused about who
they are and where they're at

00:12:32.279 --> 00:12:34.625
and they're in this dark
forest of the unknown

00:12:34.625 --> 00:12:36.625
with no plan to get out.

00:12:37.544 --> 00:12:39.045
They had no idea.

00:12:39.045 --> 00:12:40.264
They just jumped into something.

00:12:40.264 --> 00:12:43.191
They didn't study before taking that leap.

00:12:43.191 --> 00:12:45.622
And I would say, you know
what, study, pay attention,

00:12:45.622 --> 00:12:48.374
learn from the best, model
the most intelligent,

00:12:48.374 --> 00:12:51.124
smart, successful people
you can in any given area

00:12:51.124 --> 00:12:53.523
that you want to succeed in in your life

00:12:53.523 --> 00:12:54.612
before you get into it.

00:12:54.612 --> 00:12:58.499
Then, develop competency by
doing it over and over and over

00:12:58.499 --> 00:12:59.332
and over again.

00:12:59.332 --> 00:13:01.342
Don't do it once in a
while, here and there.

00:13:01.342 --> 00:13:02.798
Over and over and over.

00:13:02.798 --> 00:13:04.537
That's how you get competence.

00:13:04.537 --> 00:13:07.164
You need to get in a community
where you can get feedback.

00:13:07.164 --> 00:13:09.184
You need either a coach who
can give you some direct

00:13:09.184 --> 00:13:11.492
one-to-one feedback or a
community of friends who you just

00:13:11.492 --> 00:13:13.763
go out with, maybe you go to
lunch with them once a month.

00:13:13.763 --> 00:13:14.857
You share everything you're doing,

00:13:14.857 --> 00:13:15.993
they give you some feedback.

00:13:15.993 --> 00:13:18.384
Or you shoot a video, you send
that video out to everybody

00:13:18.384 --> 00:13:19.802
and get some feedback on it.

00:13:19.802 --> 00:13:22.914
You create a PowerPoint,
practice it with five people

00:13:22.914 --> 00:13:24.456
before the big meeting.

00:13:24.456 --> 00:13:26.646
Like, get back in the game
where you have a community

00:13:26.646 --> 00:13:28.313
of people who are giving
you advanced feedback

00:13:28.313 --> 00:13:29.940
before you release it.

00:13:29.940 --> 00:13:33.981
Feedback before you do it
so that you get smarter

00:13:33.981 --> 00:13:38.357
at all of this because nothing
makes a dream come more

00:13:38.357 --> 00:13:40.705
into life than when you
start getting feedback

00:13:40.705 --> 00:13:44.354
from other people about your
movement toward the dreams.

00:13:44.354 --> 00:13:45.187
You know?

00:13:45.187 --> 00:13:47.074
Before I shoot a big
sales video for one of

00:13:47.074 --> 00:13:50.230
my online courses, I'll
send it out to 15-20 people

00:13:50.230 --> 00:13:53.636
and get feedback and then I'll
often go re-shoot it again.

00:13:53.636 --> 00:13:55.865
Or I'll put it out into
my community and I'll see

00:13:55.865 --> 00:13:58.251
the clicks, the conversions,
and say, it's not,

00:13:58.251 --> 00:14:02.574
let's do it again and it's that
willingness to get feedback

00:14:02.574 --> 00:14:05.128
that will keep your dream
alive because, look,

00:14:05.128 --> 00:14:07.847
if it's just in your mind
and you're just doing it

00:14:07.847 --> 00:14:11.952
by yourself but you never
actually get a positive community

00:14:11.952 --> 00:14:13.953
giving you constructive
feedback towards it,

00:14:13.953 --> 00:14:17.036
it will never be in the social realm.

00:14:18.248 --> 00:14:19.709
And when it is in the social realm,

00:14:19.709 --> 00:14:21.815
it feels more real, you know?

00:14:21.815 --> 00:14:23.235
When people are actually
commenting, I mean,

00:14:23.235 --> 00:14:25.711
it's one thing to be an
artist and in your studio

00:14:25.711 --> 00:14:28.470
painting for yourself
all day, that's great.

00:14:28.470 --> 00:14:30.256
But once you get some feedback on it

00:14:30.256 --> 00:14:31.916
and constructive feedback, you become,

00:14:31.916 --> 00:14:36.380
you get that self awareness
and that social awareness

00:14:36.380 --> 00:14:39.010
to contribute and create at another level.

00:14:39.010 --> 00:14:41.772
What is it you're really after
and is it after what you,

00:14:41.772 --> 00:14:44.729
are you after enough for yourself?

00:14:44.729 --> 00:14:46.633
Are you limiting yourself based on

00:14:46.633 --> 00:14:48.293
your current competencies?

00:14:48.293 --> 00:14:49.145
A lot of people do that.

00:14:49.145 --> 00:14:51.778
They narrow they their vision
or their ambition for tomorrow

00:14:51.778 --> 00:14:55.582
based on what they can do
today or who they are today

00:14:55.582 --> 00:14:58.909
without realizing they
can develop their mastery,

00:14:58.909 --> 00:15:00.890
their skills, their
competencies, their knowledge,

00:15:00.890 --> 00:15:01.940
their experience.

00:15:01.940 --> 00:15:04.886
Without realizing it, they
can become a better person,

00:15:04.886 --> 00:15:07.754
they can live into their highest self,

00:15:07.754 --> 00:15:11.436
they can live into the type
of person who could accomplish

00:15:11.436 --> 00:15:14.648
those goals, who could have those things.

00:15:14.648 --> 00:15:16.387
So never limit your ambitions

00:15:16.387 --> 00:15:18.982
based on your current competencies.

00:15:18.982 --> 00:15:21.383
Never limit yourself today based on

00:15:21.383 --> 00:15:23.172
your current inadequacies because those

00:15:23.172 --> 00:15:25.422
can be irrelevant tomorrow.

00:15:26.331 --> 00:15:28.557
The main thing is to have aim in life.

00:15:28.557 --> 00:15:30.942
To have your own aim, to
have your own ambitions,

00:15:30.942 --> 00:15:33.449
not the ambitions somebody
told you you should have

00:15:33.449 --> 00:15:36.118
or someone told you you're
supposed to be after

00:15:36.118 --> 00:15:38.382
because that's how we all
get on sort of, you know,

00:15:38.382 --> 00:15:41.045
sometimes a corporate treadmill
or we get on those things

00:15:41.045 --> 00:15:43.379
where we just start trying to live a life

00:15:43.379 --> 00:15:44.851
that's not even our own

00:15:44.851 --> 00:15:46.980
because we're just going with everybody.

00:15:46.980 --> 00:15:48.901
But ambition liberates that.

00:15:48.901 --> 00:15:52.964
Your individual ambition,
who you want to become.

00:15:52.964 --> 00:15:55.217
What you want to do.

00:15:55.217 --> 00:15:56.905
What you want to contribute.

00:15:56.905 --> 00:15:59.663
And the highest forms of all
ambition usually come down to

00:15:59.663 --> 00:16:02.793
your creative expression,
your contribution,

00:16:02.793 --> 00:16:04.396
and your connection with others.

00:16:04.396 --> 00:16:05.229
That creative expression.

00:16:05.229 --> 00:16:08.390
What is it you want to create
in this world and, I mean,

00:16:08.390 --> 00:16:10.195
get your hands dirty doing?

00:16:10.195 --> 00:16:11.028
You know?

00:16:11.028 --> 00:16:12.995
Not just create some
PowerPoint once in a while

00:16:12.995 --> 00:16:16.323
for some corporate thing but
something real and meaningful

00:16:16.323 --> 00:16:19.277
that you consider art for
yourself, whatever that is.

00:16:19.277 --> 00:16:21.654
Even if it is a PowerPoint
presentation, right?

00:16:21.654 --> 00:16:24.739
But to do something that you
find artistic and meaningful,

00:16:24.739 --> 00:16:27.199
that's our human drive
for creative expression.

00:16:27.199 --> 00:16:29.422
Then, what about contribution?

00:16:29.422 --> 00:16:31.844
What's your ambition to give

00:16:31.844 --> 00:16:34.225
and to serve greatly for others?

00:16:34.225 --> 00:16:38.834
What do you really want to
give back or give to others?

00:16:38.834 --> 00:16:39.739
What is it?

00:16:39.739 --> 00:16:41.504
And what about connection?

00:16:41.504 --> 00:16:44.422
You know, the ultimate ambition
and aim to have, I think,

00:16:44.422 --> 00:16:46.893
for a lot of people is
their relationships.

00:16:46.893 --> 00:16:51.043
To operate and have a
love that knows no bounds,

00:16:51.043 --> 00:16:54.085
a love that is extraordinary,
that is amazing.

00:16:54.085 --> 00:16:57.087
You can't improve your
relationship with your family

00:16:57.087 --> 00:17:00.406
or your spouse or those that
you serve unless you have

00:17:00.406 --> 00:17:04.351
in some sense about you
the desire to love or give

00:17:04.351 --> 00:17:06.279
or connect more.

00:17:06.279 --> 00:17:08.126
So today, get clear.

00:17:08.126 --> 00:17:11.455
What is it that you want and
is it big enough for yourself?

00:17:11.455 --> 00:17:13.465
Not limiting yourself
based off your inadequacies

00:17:13.465 --> 00:17:17.215
or your competencies, but
based on what you truly desire.

00:17:17.215 --> 00:17:20.421
Last challenge, take whatever
that is that you come up with

00:17:20.421 --> 00:17:21.338
and 10x it.

00:17:22.420 --> 00:17:23.423
Take it by 10 times.

00:17:23.423 --> 00:17:25.317
What would be 10 times that ambition?

00:17:25.317 --> 00:17:27.701
Not just because it's silly, I know,

00:17:27.701 --> 00:17:30.082
I know it's kind of silly
but to take that ambition

00:17:30.082 --> 00:17:31.767
that you initially have, which is usually,

00:17:31.767 --> 00:17:34.193
what we usually want
is an impulse based on

00:17:34.193 --> 00:17:35.342
who we are today.

00:17:35.342 --> 00:17:38.095
And I just challenge people,
think bigger for yourself

00:17:38.095 --> 00:17:40.867
because you are immense,
you are magnificent,

00:17:40.867 --> 00:17:44.336
you are powerful beyond
your current understandings.

00:17:44.336 --> 00:17:45.817
So break through that on another level.

00:17:45.817 --> 00:17:48.279
Challenge your brain to think
even bigger for yourself.

00:17:48.279 --> 00:17:51.349
Even if it's just as an
activity to break the bounds

00:17:51.349 --> 00:17:53.604
of your current beliefs and behaviors.

00:17:53.604 --> 00:17:56.351
You deserve something
extraordinary in your life

00:17:56.351 --> 00:17:58.902
but at first, you have to want it.

00:17:58.902 --> 00:18:01.811
What makes a great person these days?

00:18:01.811 --> 00:18:04.150
What really makes someone extraordinary,

00:18:04.150 --> 00:18:05.257
what makes somebody stand out?

00:18:05.257 --> 00:18:07.509
What's going to make you
feel like you're contributing

00:18:07.509 --> 00:18:10.295
your best, like you're
making your difference,

00:18:10.295 --> 00:18:12.385
and that you're always
aspiring to be a better human

00:18:12.385 --> 00:18:13.905
but you're also achieving along the way.

00:18:13.905 --> 00:18:15.668
I would argue that that thing

00:18:15.668 --> 00:18:18.291
that makes us great is generosity.

00:18:18.291 --> 00:18:21.627
You know, the ability
to be generous to others

00:18:21.627 --> 00:18:25.328
with your time, your
attention, your mentorship,

00:18:25.328 --> 00:18:28.556
your care, your love, your
patience, your forgiveness,

00:18:28.556 --> 00:18:31.513
your understanding, your
spirit, your energy!

00:18:31.513 --> 00:18:33.567
When you are generous with who you are,

00:18:33.567 --> 00:18:36.655
people vibrate with that,
they feel it, they sense it

00:18:36.655 --> 00:18:37.720
and they're surprised by it.

00:18:37.720 --> 00:18:39.925
In a world today where no
one will even take time

00:18:39.925 --> 00:18:43.872
to say hello or to call
somebody or to show a measure

00:18:43.872 --> 00:18:47.316
of appreciation, when you
do that, you stand out

00:18:47.316 --> 00:18:50.809
but you also light up in your soul.

00:18:50.809 --> 00:18:53.109
You know, it changes
everything when you're willing

00:18:53.109 --> 00:18:54.379
to be different, when you're willing

00:18:54.379 --> 00:18:55.773
to be generous with people.

00:18:55.773 --> 00:18:58.197
Because, really, you know,
it's a very biblical thing,

00:18:58.197 --> 00:19:00.291
ask and you shall receive.

00:19:00.291 --> 00:19:03.489
I also think that in terms
of career and in terms

00:19:03.489 --> 00:19:07.845
of chasing your dreams,
give and you shall receive.

00:19:07.845 --> 00:19:08.705
You know?

00:19:08.705 --> 00:19:11.377
Give as much of your heart
and your spirit and your life

00:19:11.377 --> 00:19:14.411
and your voice to this
world, this time, this day,

00:19:14.411 --> 00:19:16.715
this person in front of you
because we only get one shot

00:19:16.715 --> 00:19:17.841
at this life.

00:19:17.841 --> 00:19:19.814
And today it never
happens, you don't see it.

00:19:19.814 --> 00:19:22.235
You know, I'm blessed to be
here and shooting this video

00:19:22.235 --> 00:19:24.617
at my writer's villa where I come to write

00:19:24.617 --> 00:19:26.094
and now shoot these episodes.

00:19:26.094 --> 00:19:28.797
And I could share with
you, you know, all this,

00:19:28.797 --> 00:19:31.956
when I got here, and what
I think about this space,

00:19:31.956 --> 00:19:34.877
it came from a position of generosity.

00:19:34.877 --> 00:19:36.735
And it came from a position
of generosity in my life

00:19:36.735 --> 00:19:40.877
so long ago when I had a high
school mentor, Mrs. Bellew,

00:19:40.877 --> 00:19:42.764
who believed in me.

00:19:42.764 --> 00:19:45.064
She saw me take some pictures
and she said, you know,

00:19:45.064 --> 00:19:46.092
those pictures are pretty good.

00:19:46.092 --> 00:19:48.397
Even though, honestly, looking
back, they were kind of crap.

00:19:48.397 --> 00:19:50.701
But she'd cheered me on anyway
because I was putting effort

00:19:50.701 --> 00:19:52.626
and she was see I was kind
of passionate about it.

00:19:52.626 --> 00:19:54.482
And she said, you know,
you could probably write,

00:19:54.482 --> 00:19:59.405
and you could probably shoot
these photographs, and I had,

00:19:59.405 --> 00:20:02.236
nobody had ever really told
me I had any potential before.

00:20:02.236 --> 00:20:03.922
And here was this person
for no reason saying

00:20:03.922 --> 00:20:06.135
you could probably do this.

00:20:06.135 --> 00:20:09.092
And I started doing it and she'd
cheer me on and cheer me on

00:20:09.092 --> 00:20:12.102
and her generosity of her time,
her effort, her mentorship,

00:20:12.102 --> 00:20:14.239
she wasn't, there was
no reason she did it,

00:20:14.239 --> 00:20:15.718
she just believed in me.

00:20:15.718 --> 00:20:19.376
But you know what, she believed
in everybody around her.

00:20:19.376 --> 00:20:22.905
She was always cheering people
on, always rewarding effort,

00:20:22.905 --> 00:20:25.079
always telling people
to pursue their passions

00:20:25.079 --> 00:20:26.107
and believe in themselves.

00:20:26.107 --> 00:20:28.776
And I'm here today, I get
to do this work with you,

00:20:28.776 --> 00:20:32.068
and millions of people see
these videos and hear me online,

00:20:32.068 --> 00:20:34.127
or watch my posts
online, or read my emails

00:20:34.127 --> 00:20:38.233
every single week because
this woman, who was a teacher,

00:20:38.233 --> 00:20:40.327
at a simple high school in a simple town

00:20:40.327 --> 00:20:43.280
with a simple, beautiful
generous spirit said,

00:20:43.280 --> 00:20:44.838
I believe in you, kid.

00:20:44.838 --> 00:20:47.710
I remember when I was going
to start my business and I

00:20:47.710 --> 00:20:49.519
really wanted to be good at it.

00:20:49.519 --> 00:20:51.706
You know, I was trying to
become and author and a speaker

00:20:51.706 --> 00:20:54.492
and do these types of videos
and do some online training

00:20:54.492 --> 00:20:57.203
for people on the topics
of motivation and marketing

00:20:57.203 --> 00:21:00.028
and, you know, all these people
were saying, well, Brendon,

00:21:00.028 --> 00:21:02.100
you may or may not be
successful with that,

00:21:02.100 --> 00:21:03.168
you're, you know, blah, blah, blah.

00:21:03.168 --> 00:21:04.766
And I thought, it's a weird thing.

00:21:04.766 --> 00:21:07.777
It's not like there's a
trait of successful people.

00:21:07.777 --> 00:21:10.490
You look across history
and successful people,

00:21:10.490 --> 00:21:12.500
it's not, they're not
from a given background,

00:21:12.500 --> 00:21:15.502
they don't come from a
specific economic stature,

00:21:15.502 --> 00:21:17.191
they're not in a position where, you know,

00:21:17.191 --> 00:21:19.461
they're at one demographic
or another demographic,

00:21:19.461 --> 00:21:20.434
I mean, it's all over.

00:21:20.434 --> 00:21:23.062
I mean, we've got thousands of
collective years of history.

00:21:23.062 --> 00:21:25.368
People succeed, some people
do, some people don't,

00:21:25.368 --> 00:21:29.222
and I think it more comes down
to how do we manage our mind?

00:21:29.222 --> 00:21:31.108
And how do we manage our days?

00:21:31.108 --> 00:21:32.996
And I think that there's a
difference between successful

00:21:32.996 --> 00:21:36.441
people and unsuccessful people
in the way that particularly

00:21:36.441 --> 00:21:39.580
think about approaching something new.

00:21:39.580 --> 00:21:42.623
You know, I think unsuccessful
people, when they have a big

00:21:42.623 --> 00:21:45.044
dream and they start thinking
about what's going to be

00:21:45.044 --> 00:21:49.179
required to accomplish that
dream, they get very limiting

00:21:49.179 --> 00:21:51.440
in their beliefs about
themselves and what's possible.

00:21:51.440 --> 00:21:54.099
And specifically they say
three types of things.

00:21:54.099 --> 00:21:56.358
You know, the first thing they
often say is well, you know,

00:21:56.358 --> 00:21:57.999
I don't know how to do that.

00:21:57.999 --> 00:21:59.893
So they stop.

00:21:59.893 --> 00:22:03.340
They say, you know, I
don't have those things.

00:22:03.340 --> 00:22:05.068
So they stop.

